  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\fundamental.theorem.of.calculus]\nTheorem:\ngiven:\n. a, b is \\real\n. f, F is \\function:on{\\reals}:to{\\reals}\nwhere:\n. a \\:real.less?:/ b\n. forAll: x is \\real\n  then: \\derivative:of{F}:at{x} = f(x)\nthen: \\riemann.integral:of{f}:on{a, b} = F(b) \\.real.-./ F(a)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Fundamental Theorem of Calculus\"\n. description: \"If $F$ is an antiderivative of continuous $f$, then\n                $\\int_a^b f(x) dx = F(b) - F(a)$.\"\nId: \"17d7c6be-11d7-44bf-b522-515557063ed7\"",
